Prompt 3 - Code review of part 1 (/code-review), then fix all findings
---------------------------------------------------------------------
Request: review the code of part 1 only (no changes to part 2 / proteomics); then "fix all ten,
rerun the tests and commit".
Findings and fixes (all in part1_haplograph/):
  1. Evo 2 is kept in bf16, so in-place AdamW updates at lr 1e-5 round away and "fine-tuned"
     blocks never change. evo2_model.fit now optimizes fp32 master copies (MasterWeights) and
     writes them back each step. Checked: after 160 steps a bf16 layer changed 208/256 weights
     with master copies vs 0/256 with in-place updates.
  2. Step 3 reused embeddings / SVD caches after a graph rebuild in the same folder. Outputs now
     record graph_id (hash of graph_info.json); caches include it; step 4 refuses stale embeddings.
  3. Step 1 silently kept an existing graph built with other settings. It now compares chromosomes,
     --edges, --min-lift and train/test set ids with graph_info.json and stops on a mismatch
     (--force rebuilds, --out writes elsewhere).
  4. 4b did not validate --val-frac (crash with 1.0). Added the check and an empty-train guard.
  5. Step 1 with --train-individuals wrote no test file, so step 5 fell back to BH_26 half_B
     (possible overlap). Step 1 now takes the split's test file when the train file is the split's
     own and warns otherwise; step 5 refuses a graph with a training set but no test file.
  6. URL downloads were cached by file name and could resolve to a local file of the same name.
     Now cached under downloads/<hash of URL>/ (haplo_common.url_cache_path).
  7. Step 4 --chroms 21,22 failed (no chr prefix). Uses parse_chroms like the other scripts.
  8. Step 5 loaded the checkpoint twice; it now creates the Model once and shares it.
  9. Step 0 re-hashed every cached file on each run; verified files are recorded (size, mtime) in
     raw/verified.json and skipped.
  10. Duplicated code: 4a and 4b now share evo2_model.fit / config_of; step 5 uses haplo_common's
      log, is_url, download and read_graph_individuals.
Docs: README (own "Now:" note on the step-5 fallback) and DOCUMENTATION updated for 1, 2, 3, 5, 9.
Tests: all six --test flags pass; targeted checks for every fix; the real chr21 pipeline rerun on CPU.

Prompt 4 - Three improvement iterations on part 1 (brainstorm -> code review -> spec-tester)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Request: iterate 3 times; each time run /hackathon-brainstorm on the CURRENT part 1 (not from
scratch) and implement its suggestions, run /code-review on the modified code and apply its
findings, then run the spec-tester agent on part 1 and fix the inconsistencies it finds. Leave
part 2 entirely alone.

Iteration 1
  Brainstorm: 10 hypotheses scored; pursued H1 (held-out co-occurrence test of the embeddings),
  H2 (paired bootstrap CIs over test individuals), H3 (bigram conditional entropy floor), H4
  (region-conditioned accuracy); H5-H7 deferred to later iterations, H8-H10 dropped. Plan written to
  part1_haplograph/IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md and PROMPTS.md (README.md not overwritten: the skill's
  README/requirements outputs were redirected there; no new dependencies).
  Implemented: 5_validate_evo2.py task embedding_cooccurrence (AUC of embedding cosine for test-set
  co-occurrence, distance-matched, references: genomic proximity and train lift); test_set_performance
  gained paired bootstrap CIs, region-conditioned top-1 and the bigram entropy floor;
  validation_tasks.txt and DOCUMENTATION.md updated.
  First chr21 result: co-occurrence AUC XGBoost 0.713, node2vec 0.546, GNN 0.534 (later shown to be
  a cluster-frequency artifact, see code review).
  Code review (10 findings, all fixed in 5_validate_evo2.py): (1) warn when the graph used test
  individuals (AUC not held-out); (2) distinct pairs and a bootstrap over haploblock regions instead
  of over correlated pairs; (3) the bigram entropy is a reference, not a floor (renamed
  bigram_reference_entropy, test_loss_minus_bigram_reference); (4) labels were dominated by cluster
  frequency: pairs now need >= min_expected (5) expected test co-carriers, plus frequency-matched AUC
  and a cluster-frequency reference; (5) the self-test now asserts CI coverage, region top-1 >= top-1,
  proximity ~0.5, train lift and GNN > 0.5; (6) mismatched embedding files reported in notes; (7)
  embedding_cooccurrence only in the default task list when embeddings exist, skips instead of
  failing; (8) docstring outputs updated; (9) region-conditioned top-1 counts ties as misses; (10)
  one random generator per task.
  Corrected chr21 result (3,228 pairs, 116 positive): GNN 0.978, XGBoost 0.968, node2vec 0.881,
  train-lift reference 0.991, proximity 0.618, cluster frequency 0.354. Bigram top-1 0.418
  [0.410, 0.426]; bigram reference entropy 1.82 nats.
  Spec-tester (9 findings, all fixed; 13 regression tests added in part1_haplograph/tests/, all pass):
    1. HIGH security: step 5 fell back to torch.load(weights_only=False), so a crafted .pt ran code.
       Now weights_only=True only; anything else is refused.
    2. HIGH leakage: steps 3/4 accepted any --train-individuals (even the test set). train_columns now
       refuses any set other than the graph's; embedding_cooccurrence marks embeddings from another
       training set as not held-out; model_info also counts test individuals among val_individuals.
    3. --gwas replaced the default step-5 tasks; it now adds to them (docstring updated).
    4. Step 5 did not check a model's graph build / embeddings; load_finetuned now fails the task.
    5. Step 1's per-chromosome cache ignored --raw-dir / re-downloads; now keyed by raw file
       (path, size, mtime).
    6. Nemotron: relative/Windows paths and non-1000G sample names leaked, the key went to any URL
       incl. http and across redirects. Now: directories scrubbed, file-name/column fields dropped,
       graph individual names scrubbed, https or localhost only, redirects not followed.
    7. Step 3 reused embeddings after settings changed; outputs now record a settings id; the
       features cache includes seed and RAPIDS sample size.
    8. Step 0 kept old half_A/B.txt when --splits-url changed; downloads now cached per URL.
    9. Minor: step 1 --test-individuals URL cached in the workdir (not shared /tmp); the training loop
       no longer drops the last partial batch; clear errors for truncated/malformed nodes files,
       non-0/1 carriers, bad task lines and permutations=0; install_evo2.sh gets EVO2_REF and tests
